
"smart_sources:ba4whk2q8.txt": {"path":"ba4whk2q8.txt","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"od8we5","at":1785795035860},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1774844714492,"size":115327,"at":1785795035861,"hash":"od8we5"},"blocks":{"#":[1,31]},"outlinks":[{"title":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Posted to LAF-7. Here's the full return:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Moved\\nNothing. Inspect-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Trigger-chain risk\\n\\nThree distinct states, each with a different failure mode:\\n\\n| State | Trigger | Failure |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Current `main` | Direct `pull_request:` ✓ | `LINEAR_API_KEY` missing — exits 1 on every run |\\n| Codex LAF-15 merges as-is | **Two** direct `pull_request:` triggers | Race — both v1 and v2 write to the same Linear issue simultaneously |\\n| PR #96 merges as-is | `workflow_call:` only, no caller | Silent — no PR events trigger anything |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Duplicate-workflow risk\\n\\nCodex LAF-15 branch adds `pr-linear-sync.yml` alongside `linear-pr-sync.yml` (v1 not deleted). Both have identical trigger conditions. Before that branch merges, v1 must be deleted. Codex owns this.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Corrected from earlier brief\\n\\n`LINEAR_PR_OPEN_STATE_ID` / `LINEAR_PR_MERGED_STATE_ID` are **not hard blockers** — `linear_pr_sync.py` skips state updates gracefully if they're absent. Not a merge gate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Uncommitted local changes worth surfacing\\n\\nOn `claude/resolve-pr-conflicts`, staged but not committed:\\n- [.github/workflows/linear-brief.yml","target":".github/workflows/linear-brief.yml","line":8},{"title":".github/workflows/vault-ingest.yml","target":".github/workflows/vault-ingest.yml","line":8}],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},